            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI don't think I see autocommand picker as sufficiently useful (and used) to be included in 'mini.extra'. Also because it would require quite a lot of testing because there are many filtering options to autocommands available.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nHere is a rough outline of how this can be implemented manually:\r\n- Use `vim.api.nvim_get_autocmds({})` to get an array of autocommand data. Replace `{}` with filtering options it accepts (`group`, `event`, `pattern`, `buffer`).\r\n- Enrich array elements with data so that they are useful ['mini.pick' items](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/061379f082d6b03305b00ddd6f8f6b7b8eded6d8/doc/mini-pick.txt#L223-L281). One tricky thing might be to get the position of where the autocommand is defined, which can be achieved through `debug.getinfo()` on the `callback` field (similar to [how it is done in `MiniExtra.pickers.keymaps()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/061379f082d6b03305b00ddd6f8f6b7b8eded6d8/lua/mini/extra.lua#L991-L997)).",
